extends ../../webinc/html/disease.jade

block head
    title Dental Plaque - Plants Cause Disease

block content
    h1 Dental Plaque
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/10953-plaque") Cleveland Clinic]:
    blockquote Dental plaque is a sticky film of bacteria that constantly forms on your teeth. It’s normal to produce plaque. But if you don’t remove plaque with routine dental cleanings and daily brushing and flossing, it can cause cavities, gum disease and other oral health issues.
